  "question": {
    "text": "A particle of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;with an initial velocity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;collides perfectly elastically with a mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;at rest. It moves with a velocity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;after collision, then,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></math>&nbsp;is given by&nbsp;",
